        "text": "# Off-By-One Error\n\nAn **off-by-one error** is a programming mistake where a loop runs one time too many or one time too few.\n\n**Example**: Using `i <= 3` instead of `i < 3` makes the loop run 4 times instead of 3, causing one extra loop cycle.\n",
